    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      375.25,
      539.92,
      398.32
    ],
    "text": "REGULATIONS made by the President under Section 64 of the Mines and Minerals Act, No. 33 of 1992 read withSection 51 of the Nineteenth Amendment to the Constitution.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      416.05,
      539.47,
      462.16
    ],
    "text": "MAITHRIPALA SIRISENA,President.Colombo,3rd February, 2016.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      268.77,
      474.49,
      319.05,
      485.56
    ],
    "text": "Regulations",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      47.85,
      497.89,
      539.85,
      520.72
    ],
    "text": "The Mining (Licensing) regulatiom, No. 1 of 1993 published in Gazette Extraordinary No. 794/23 of November26, 1993, as amended from time to time, is hereby further amended in regulation 42 as follows :",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      89.25,
      533.05,
      539.92,
      555.76
    ],
    "text": "(1) by the repeal of the definition of the expression \u201cbuilding materials\u201d and the substitution therefor of thefollowing definition :",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      119.85,
      568.09,
      539.79,
      590.92
    ],
    "text": "\u201cbuilding materials\u201d include sand, gravel, soil, laterite, dolomite used for construction industry, shale,rock aggregates and clays which are used for production of brick and tile ;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      91.29,
      603.25,
      539.89,
      625.96
    ],
    "text": "(2) by the repeal of the definition of the expression \u201cindustrial minerals\u201d and the substitution therefor of thefollowing definition :",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      119.85,
      638.29,
      539.95,
      684.52
    ],
    "text": "\u201cindustrial minerals\u201d mean ilmenite, zircon, rutile, monazite, coral, shells beds, graphite, ball clay, ceramicand cement clay, kaolin, mica, feldspar, limestone, salt, gypsum, ochre, silica sand (glass sand), quartz,garnet, silimanite, calcite, allanite, fluorspar, serpentinite, apatite, dolomite used for fertilizer, magnetite,magnesite, peat, wallastonite and dimension stone,\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
